Subject: [PATCH] prioritize native control traffic and retain transient radio updates

Assign Linux 802.1D user priority 7 to the alternative raw Ethernet sender.
AL-SAP builds use ieee1905-em patch 0008 instead. The lab bridge classifier
must restore this priority after veth forwarding and at wireless relay hops.
The traffic still crosses the real wireless backhaul, including contention,
loss and retransmissions. Priority-aware radio admission must be enabled in
the virtual medium; this is not an out-of-band metrics shortcut.

Accept radio callbacks during post-onboarding transient states, including a
pending candidate report. The callback is authoritative even when a metrics
transaction temporarily owns the radio; do not silently drop its channel report.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/em/em.cpp b/src/em/em.cpp
index dd30589..6184779 100644
--- a/src/em/em.cpp
+++ b/src/em/em.cpp
@@ -854,6 +854,15 @@ int em_t::send_frame(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int len, bool multicast)
         return -1;
     }
 
+    const int control_priority = 256 + 7;
+    if (setsockopt(sock, SOL_SOCKET, SO_PRIORITY, &control_priority,
+                   sizeof(control_priority)) < 0) {
+        em_printfout("Could not assign IEEE 1905 network-control priority: %s",
+                     strerror(errno));
+        close(sock);
+        return -1;
+    }
+
     sadr_ll.sll_ifindex = static_cast<int>(if_nametoindex(ifname));
     sadr_ll.sll_halen = ETH_ALEN; // length of destination mac address
     sadr_ll.sll_protocol = htons(ETH_P_ALL);
